!!! Hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations must never be switched off. Not in any block, not for any reason.

## When to use

Use this runbook when the day-ahead forecast or live demand reaches 92% of available supply (5200 MW).

! A stage is declared by the Duty Director, never by a single operator.

## Stages

table = stage,demand level,actions; Stage 1,"92% of supply (4784 MW)","Issue a conservation alert by text and app to 380,000 customers; ask large industrial customers on interruptible contracts to get ready to reduce load on 30 minutes of notice; confirm that standby generation at 3 peaking plants can start within 20 minutes"; Stage 2,"97% of supply (5044 MW)","Call the demand response program (about 210 MW); start buying emergency imports from the neighboring utility; brief the regulator by phone"; Stage 3,"100% of supply (5200 MW)","Begin rotating outages in blocks A to L, each block off for at most 60 minutes, in order; never repeat a block before all twelve have been used"

## Steps for rotating outages

1. Get approval
-- The Duty Director approves in the log.
-- The regulator is told within 30 minutes.
2. Protect critical sites
-- Confirm that hospitals, the 911 center and water pumping stations are excluded.
-- Check that the exclusion list was updated this month.
3. Run the blocks
-- Open the first block's feeders.
-- Restore it after 60 minutes at most and open the next.
-- Update the public outage map every 15 minutes.
4. Stand down
-- End rotating outages when demand stays below 95% for 60 minutes.
-- Restore all blocks.
-- File the event report within 24 hours.

